# Search scope — Peaky Finders

Peaky work lives in **`peaky_finders/`**. Enterprise routing: `ops/.cursor/rules/search-scope.mdc`. **Always pass an explicit path** to grep, glob, and codebase search. Do not search unscoped across sibling workspace roots.

## Default search roots

| Topic | Path | Examples |
|-------|------|----------|
| RF engine, coverage, links, DEM | `splatter/` | `Session::run`, propagate |
| HTTP serve, warm queue, viewshed | `crates/peaky-serve/` | `warm.rs`, `viewshed.rs`, `api.rs` |
| Preset YAML model, init | `crates/peaky-preset/` | `SimulationConfig`, `load_preset` |
| `peaky find path` | `crates/peaky-finder/` | route, search, chain |
| Link solver API + UI | `crates/peaky-serve/src/link_solver.rs`, `assets/static/project-map/domains/link-solver.js` | scan, accept, like |
| Geo / eligible land | `crates/peaky-geo/` | land fetch, polygonize |
| CLI entry | `cmd/peaky/` | `serve`, `find` |
| Static UI assets | `assets/` | `home-settings.js`, templates |

**Project data** (sites, `config.yaml`, land caches) lives in the **project leaf** (e.g. `peaky-nevada/`), not in this repo.

## When to widen

Search outside this repo only for cross-leaf integration (project YAML, ops initiatives, meshenvy.org map). Name the target path in the tool call.

## Anti-patterns

- Unscoped search when open files or MEMORY already imply `splatter/` or `peaky-serve/`.
- Searching all of `meshenvy/` for Peaky symbols.
- Confusing v4 Python (`peaky-finders-v4/`) with v5 Rust — port reference only, not runtime search target.
